.TH HELLO 1
.SH NAME
hello \- show its arguments and who it runs as
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hello
.RI [ word ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hello
was the first program loaded from the disk. It prints its process
number, its user number and its arguments:
.PP
.nf
Hello from the disk! I am pid 21, uid 1000, with 2 arguments: a b
.fi
.PP
Its source is also on every disk, in
.BR /src/sieos ,
to be built on SIEOS with
.BR make (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cc (1),
.BR make (1)
